+# AI Square IT Solutions
+
+Full-stack platform for AI Square IT Solutions: a public website, an employee portal, and an admin console for managing evaluators, guidelines, assessments, and hiring.
+
+## Features
+
+- Public website with careers, contact, privacy, and terms pages
+- Employee portal for guidelines, assessments, results, readiness, announcements, and feedback
+- Candidate exam portal for assigned screening assessments
+- Admin console for employees, admins, guidelines, question banks, assessments, results, readiness, applications, announcements, and activity logs
+- SQLite persistence with file storage for resumes and guideline PDFs
+- Cookie/session authentication with role-based access control
+
+## Stack
+
+- Node.js 20+
+- Express 4
+- React 18 + Vite 6
+- SQLite via `better-sqlite3`
+
+## Local development
+
+```bash
+npm ci
+npm run dev
+```
+
+The server starts on `http://localhost:3000` by default. In development, Vite runs in middleware mode through the Express server.
+
+## Production build
+
+```bash
+npm ci
+npm run build
+npm start
+```
+
+The client is built into `client_bundle/`, and the Express server serves it in production.
+
+## Environment variables
+
+| Variable | Purpose | Default |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `PORT` | HTTP port | `3000` |
+| `HOST` | Bind address | `0.0.0.0` |
+| `NODE_ENV` | `development` or `production` | unset |
+| `ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN` | Optional one-time token for creating the first admin | generated into `data/.bootstrap_token` if absent |
+| `AISQUARE_DATA_DIR` | SQLite database directory | `./data` |
+| `AISQUARE_STORAGE_DIR` | Uploaded file storage directory | `./storage` |
+
+On first run, if no admin exists, open `/admin/login` and use the bootstrap token to create the initial administrator. If `ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN` is not set, the server writes a generated token to `data/.bootstrap_token`.
+
+For production, persist `AISQUARE_DATA_DIR` and `AISQUARE_STORAGE_DIR` outside the ephemeral application filesystem.
+
+## Deployment
+
+### Docker
+
+```bash
+docker build -t aisquare-v2 .
+docker run -p 3000:3000 \
+  -e ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=your-setup-token \
+  -v aisquare-data:/app/data \
+  -v aisquare-storage:/app/storage \
+  aisquare-v2
+```
+
+### Render
+
+The repository includes `render.yaml` for a Node web service. You can also deploy using the `Dockerfile`. Set `ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN` and attach persistent storage for `/app/data` and `/app/storage` if using Docker.
+
+### Railway
+
+The repository includes `railway.json`. Set `ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN` and configure persistent storage for the data and upload directories.
+
+## Verification
+
+```bash
+npm run build
+npm run verify
+```
+
+Additional checks:
+
+```bash
+node scripts/verify-full-platform.js
+node scripts/verify-exam-portal-e2e.js
+```
+
+`server/scripts/verify-core.js` expects a running local server on port 3000 and uses the configured local data directory.
+
+## Project structure
+
+```text
+src/               React client
+server/            Express API, database, auth, and utilities
+server/db/         SQLite schema and database setup
+server/routes/     Public, auth, employee, and admin API routes
+scripts/           Build/runtime verification scripts
+client_bundle/     Production client build output
+data/              SQLite database (generated)
+storage/           Uploaded resumes and guidelines (generated)
+```
